Q41|ACCIDENTAL|GENERIC|3|process.go:176;process.go:98|swagger.yaml#624;swagger.yaml#696|Output cleanup conversion lacks PurgeOnDelete, leaving false despite copying it on input. The GET contract exposes shared process schemas; explicit Add/Update wording is attached to the separate config endpoint.
Q42|ACCIDENTAL|SPECIFIC|3|crud.go:573|bundle.yaml#583|Segment deletion uses segmentID without restricting flag membership; flagID only drives mutation bookkeeping. The operation explicitly requires flagID within its nested path.
Q43|ACCIDENTAL|GENERIC|3|VulnerabilityResource.java:139;VulnerabilityQueryManager.java:461;VulnerabilityDao.java:391|VulnerabilityResource.java#101;PaginatedApi.java#38|The DAO query lacks outer pagination and its entire list becomes the response. Pagination is promised through the reused PaginatedApi annotation, not dedicated component-operation prose.
Q44|DELIBERATE|SPECIFIC|3|api.go:585;api.go:606;api.go:1144|swagger.yml#507|The handler explicitly wraps identifiers in apiAllKeys, whose JSON property is keys. Operation prose and response schema explicitly promise an array of key identifiers.
Q45|ACCIDENTAL|SPECIFIC|2|ParameterContextResource.java:731;ParameterContextResource.java:177;ParameterContextResource.java:749|ParameterContextResource.java#663|The callback checks context, affected components, and controller-service references, but omits inherited-context read checks. Dedicated security requirements explicitly cover current and new inherited contexts; downstream authorization internals are absent.
Q46|ACCIDENTAL|SPECIFIC|3|server.go:63;handler_verify.go:428;authelia_context.go:56|openapi.yml#115|HEAD uses VerifyGet; malformed URL handling writes an error body without setting a failure status. HEAD documentation explicitly assigns 200 to success and 401 to unauthorized access.
Q47|DELIBERATE|SPECIFIC|3|server.go:601;diskfs.go:46|swagger.json#297|Explicit routes bind slashless disk listing to ListFiles and slash-wildcard requests to GetFile. The contract explicitly declares the listing path with a trailing slash.
Q48|ACCIDENTAL|SPECIFIC|3|crud.go:77;crud.go:102;scope.go:592;utils.go:128|bundle.yaml#59|The handler puts false into a value struct; the vendored query builder omits blank fields and defines false as blank. Dedicated parameter prose promises the supplied enabled status.
Q49|DELIBERATE|SPECIFIC|2|ContentFeedController.java:109;WebMvcAutoConfiguration.java:141|ContentFeedController.java#109|The handler selects a template view and the resolver explicitly sets text/html. The endpoint annotation explicitly declares text/plain. Framework view-resolution code is not supplied.
Q50|DELIBERATE|SPECIFIC|3|server.go:555;server.go:579|swagger.yml#1009|The router explicitly registers DELETE under singular org/keys/{keyName} beneath /tyk. The contract explicitly places the operation under plural orgs/keys/{keyID}.
Q51|ACCIDENTAL|SPECIFIC|2|DefaultClientApi.java:75;DefaultClientService.java:59;MapStructClientModelMapper.java:33|ClientRepresentation.java#24;ClientRepresentation.java#38;ClientRepresentation.java#42|PATCH delegates to toModel, which lacks reverse mappings for renamed fields despite forward mappings. Contract property descriptions explicitly define their meanings; generated mapper output is absent.
Q52|DELIBERATE|GENERIC|3|PositionResource.java:49;Position.java:289;Network.java:23|swagger.json#1505|Position explicitly declares a Network bean with public getters, producing an object when present. The string requirement comes from the shared Position schema.
Q53|DELIBERATE|GENERIC|3|ChatStreamHandler.java:227;ChatRequestBody.java:148;ChatApiHelper.java:245;V2ErrorCode.java:29|openapi-user.yaml#1551|The streaming handler explicitly catches the length exception and returns INVALID_REQUEST; the default limit is 4000. The contract requires message but omits any maximum length.
Q54|DELIBERATE|SPECIFIC|3|handler.go:285;handler.go:391|api.swagger.json#503;api.swagger.json#535;engine/ladon/handler.go#266|The router explicitly requires :member and the handler reads it. Contract route documentation and its body parameter explicitly describe removal through the members collection.
Q55|DELIBERATE|SPECIFIC|3|SearchApiManager.java:802;SearchApiManager.java:817|openapi-user.yaml#595|The writer explicitly emits query_time, record_count, page_size, and labels. The operation's inline response schema explicitly names took, total, num, and field.
Q56|ACCIDENTAL|SPECIFIC|2|engine/ladon/handler.go:292;storage/handler.go:85;storage/handler.go:125|api.swagger.json#494|Filtering declares a nil Roles result, appending only matches, and forwards it without empty-array initialization. The operation explicitly declares an array; external JSON writer internals are absent.
Q57|DELIBERATE|GENERIC|3|ReportResource.java:96;Position.java:289;Network.java:23|swagger.json#1505|The route returns Positions, whose network field explicitly uses the Network bean and its getters. The string requirement is inherited from the shared Position schema.
Q58|DELIBERATE|SPECIFIC|3|links.go:243;album.go:1041;link.go:262|swagger.json#88|The handler explicitly serializes m.Links(), a share-link collection. The operation explicitly declares one entity.Link object as the successful response.
